a Python package structure and ensuring it is importable by client modules.\n\n**9. Security Considerations**\n\nThe function operates purely on string manipulation, reducing direct security risks. It adheres to the principle of \"Trust the caller's inputs,\" so no explicit input validation or error raising is performed.\n\n**10. Future Work and Enhancements**\n\n*   **Error Reporting:** Introduce options to raise exceptions for malformed or unbalanced top-level input if strict parsing is required.\n*   **Configurable Ignored Characters:** Allow users to specify additional characters to ignore besides spaces.\n*   **Support for Other Delimiters:** Extend the functionality to separate groups defined by other types of brackets (e.g., `[]`, `{}`).\n\n**11. Conclusion**\n\nThe `separate_paren_groups` function offers a robust and efficient solution for extracting top-level, balanced parenthesis groups from a string. Its design prioritizes clarity, maintainability, and direct implementation of the specified requirements, handling spaces and other extraneous characters gracefully.\n\n---\n\n**File Tree:**\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 paren_utils/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 separate_groups.py\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 tests/\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_separate_groups.py\n```\n\n---\n\n**Code Implementation:**\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Separates groups of nested parentheses into individual balanced strings.\n    Ignores spaces and non-parenthesis characters in the input string.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    groups = []\n    current_group_chars = []\n    balance = 0\n    \n    for char in paren_string:\n        if char == ' ':\n            continue\n        \n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n            current_group_chars.append(char)\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n            curr